Ed has a notably critical view of Playwright in traditional IT environments. Here's his key perspective:

Core Concerns:
- Ed strongly dislikes automated testing tools like Playwright and Selenium in traditional IT environments [edhonour_DHvr8nZuZQj].
- He believes organizations that replaced skilled testing teams with these automated tools and shifted responsibility to developers are making a significant mistake [edhonour_DHvr8nZuZQj].

Specific Issues:
- Developers often spend more time writing automated test scripts than the actual code itself [edhonour_DHvr8nZuZQj].
- These tools are particularly problematic when testing AI systems because AI testing requires subjective evaluation that can't be automated [edhonour_DHvr8nZuZQj].

